* models.lib: behavioural models for the benches in run.py (ngspice 46).
*
* None of these is a vendor model. Each is built from the datasheet numbers
* quoted next to it; what a datasheet does not give is a parameter and the
* benches sweep it. SIMULATION.md says what each model can and cannot show.
*
* Copyright (C) 2026 ReBirth contributors. GPL-3.0-or-later.

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ MCP6004
* One channel of the MCP6004 (Microchip DS21733, MCP6001/2/4), generic
* rail-to-rail in/out macro-model:
*   GBW 1 MHz, SR 0.6 V/us, AOL 112 dB typ, VOS +-4.5 mV max (parameter),
*   input common mode VSS-0.3 .. VDD+0.3 V, input C 6 pF CM / 3 pF diff,
*   output within 25 mV of a rail at RL = 10 k to VDD/2 (here: 5 mV hard
*   limit + RO), short-circuit current +-23 mA at 5.5 V.
* Not in the datasheet, so parameters: FP2, the second pole (PM at G = +1
* is given as 90 deg typ, so FP2 >> GBW; 4 MHz is pessimistic), and RO, the
* open-loop output resistance.
.subckt MCP6004G inp inn out vdd vss params: VOS=0 RO=100 FP2=4e6
Cinp inp vss 6p
Cinn inn vss 6p
Cdif inp inn 3p
Dip1 inp vdd DESD
Dip2 vss inp DESD
Din1 inn vdd DESD
Din2 vss inn DESD
Emid mid 0 vol='(V(vdd)+V(vss))/2'
* transconductance stage, current limited: SR = 0.6 mA / 1 nF = 0.6 V/us
Bgm mid n1 I='6e-4*tanh((V(inp)-V(inn)+VOS)*6.2832e-3/6e-4)'
* dominant pole: gm*R1 = 4e5 (112 dB), 2.5 Hz, GBW = gm/(2 pi C1) = 1 MHz
R1 n1 mid 6.366e7
C1 n1 mid 1n
* keep the integrator near the rails in saturation (no long wind-up)
Ehi chi 0 vol='V(vdd)+0.3'
Elo clo 0 vol='V(vss)-0.3'
Dhi n1 chi DCLMP
Dlo clo n1 DCLMP
* second pole
E2 n2a 0 n1 0 1
R2 n2a n2 1k
C2 n2 0 {1/(6.2832*1k*FP2)}
* output: 5 mV from either rail, then RO with a +-23 mA current limit
Bo n3 0 V='min(max(V(n2), V(vss)+5m), V(vdd)-5m)'
Bro n3 out I='23m*tanh((V(n3)-V(out))/(RO*23m))'
Do1 out vdd DESD
Do2 vss out DESD
.model DCLMP D(IS=1e-12 N=0.1)
.model DESD D(IS=1e-15 N=1 RS=5)
.ends MCP6004G

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ logic buffers
* Push-pull CMOS output: threshold VTH on the input, edge time TE, output
* resistance ROUT. Rail = vcc.
*   74AHCT125 on VBUS: TTL input (VIH 2.0 / VIL 0.8 V, VTH ~1.5 V), VOH >= 3.94 V
*     at -8 mA and VOL <= 0.36 V at 8 mA with VCC = 4.5 V -> ROUT <= 70 / 45 R.
*   74LVC1G14 on +3V3: VOL <= 0.55 V at 24 mA, VOH >= 2.3 V at -24 mA (VCC 3 V)
*     -> ROUT <= 23 R sinking, <= 30 R sourcing.
.subckt CMOSBUF in out vcc gnd params: VTH=1.5 TE=2n ROUT=40
Bsw int gnd V='V(vcc,gnd)*(0.5+0.5*tanh((V(in,gnd)-VTH)/0.05))'
Rte int int2 1
Cte int2 gnd {TE/2.2}
Rout int2 out {ROUT}
.ends CMOSBUF

* Inverting version (74LVC1G14: Schmitt inverter; the UART edge is clean, so the
* hysteresis does not matter here).
.subckt CMOSINV in out vcc gnd params: VTH=1.65 TE=2n ROUT=20
Bsw int gnd V='V(vcc,gnd)*(0.5-0.5*tanh((V(in,gnd)-VTH)/0.05))'
Rte int int2 1
Cte int2 gnd {TE/2.2}
Rout int2 out {ROUT}
.ends CMOSINV

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ transistors
* MMBT3904 = 2N3904 die in SOT-23. The classic 2N3904 model (as published by
* National/Fairchild and shipped with most SPICE libraries).
.model Q2N3904 NPN(IS=6.734f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF=416.4 NE=1.259 ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m
+ XTB=1.5 BR=.7371 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1 CJC=3.638p MJC=.3085 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=4.493p
+ MJE=.2593 VJE=.75 TR=239.5n TF=301.2p ITF=.4 VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ diodes
* 1N4148W (D401, receiver protection diodes)
.model D1N4148 D(IS=2.52n RS=0.568 N=1.752 CJO=4p M=0.4 TT=20n BV=100 IBV=100u)
* opto input LEDs (GaAs IR). VF fitted to the datasheet points:
*   6N138 (Broadcom/Vishay): VF 1.4 V typ / 1.7 V max at IF = 1.6 mA
*   H11L1: VF 1.2 V typ / 1.5 V max at IF = 10 mA
.model LED6N138 D(IS=1.2e-14 N=2.1 RS=1 CJO=30p)
.model LED6N138MAX D(IS=4.9e-17 N=2.1 RS=1 CJO=30p)
.model LEDH11L1 D(IS=9.5e-13 N=2.0 RS=1 CJO=30p)
* CA-033's worst receiver LED: 1.9 V forward drop (PC900V class) at ~4.5 mA
.model LEDVF19 D(IS=2.9e-18 N=2.1 RS=1 CJO=30p)
.model LEDH11L1MAX D(IS=5.8e-15 N=2.0 RS=1 CJO=30p)

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ ferrite bead
* 1 kOhm at 100 MHz, 0603 (MMZ1608Y102B class): DCR ~0.35 R, inductive below
* ~30 MHz, resistive at 100 MHz. Only its low-frequency part matters here.
.subckt FB1K a b
Rdc a m 0.35
L1 m b 1.5u
Rp m b 1k
.ends FB1K

* ------------------------------------------------------------------ MIDI cable
* One 5 m section of shielded twisted pair, pins 4 and 5 (loop): 0.5 uH/m loop
* inductance, 80 pF/m between the wires, 0.17 R/m loop resistance.
.subckt MIDICAB5M a4 a5 b4 b5
R4 a4 m4 0.43
L4 m4 b4 1.25u
R5 a5 m5 0.43
L5 m5 b5 1.25u
C1 a4 a5 200p
C2 b4 b5 200p
.ends MIDICAB5M
